	Basically, the Emacs could not find the GCC paths
	The instruction it gave was to paste the following snippet into ~/.emacs.d/early-init.el file:
(when (eq system-type 'darwin)
  ;; Ensure Homebrew binary paths are available to Emacs
  (let ((homebrew-bin "/opt/homebrew/bin"))
    (when (file-directory-p homebrew-bin)
      (setenv "PATH" (concat homebrew-bin ":" (getenv "PATH")))
      (setq exec-path (cons homebrew-bin exec-path))))

  ;; Provide the specific paths for libgccjit to find the compiler driver
  (setenv "LIBRARY_PATH" 
          (string-join 
           '("/opt/homebrew/lib/gcc/current"
             "/opt/homebrew/opt/gcc/lib/gcc/current"
             "/opt/homebrew/opt/libgccjit/lib/gcc/current") 
           ":")))

There was one warning after:
	Warning (files): Missing ‘lexical-binding’ cookie in "~/.emacs.d/early-init.el".
