Problem 5

1. https://sunpy.org/
The software package ‘sunpy’ is used for data analysis in solar physics. 
It started out at NASA’s Goddard Spaceflight Center but has grown to be used 
by the wider solar physicist’s community. It utilizes Python packages such as 
pandas, numpy, astropy, scipy, and matplotlib. Its functionality includes 
retrieving and downloading data from major sources, using solar coordinate 
systems and transformations, and interfacing with and visualizing solar data. 

2. https://github.com/nugent-lab/FindPOTATOs-stable/
The software ‘FindPOTATOs’ is used to link together observations of minor 
planets into tracklets (a series of images showing the body moving against 
the star background). It’s useful for processing data from archives and small 
observatories. It’s a general algorithm that can be used for a range of bodies 
from near-Earth objects to Trans-Neptunian objects. It utilizes Python packages 
such as pandas, numpy, astropy, astroquery, and matplotlib.

