In class 
Listening to zoom lecture

Think-pair-share measurement tape
- If it's in half-inches then units are wrong, and need to be converted: illegitimate
- The tape has to be in the right direction so vertical - random
- If the tape is too short then need to note where the end was correctly - illegitimate
- Not staring at zero - systematic



Illegitimate, systematic, random
Thermal expansion - systematic
Time of day - random unless you can model it, then systematic

Examples
Illegitimate: take data of the wrong star
Systematic: from scale calibration, observation bias 
Random: I said cosmic rays, but that was wrong. 

