In class
 
N-m : m is degrees of freedom
So how many pieces of info we used to fit the data
for quadratic: ax^2 +bx +c
a, b, c --> 3 pieces of info
m = 3

For discrete 
p(x) is described by dirac delta function

Poisson
prob of observing some number of events in one time interval out of n possible events, each has a prob p of occurring

for astronomy n>>>>1

t is length of time waiting
Tau is rate
n is av events per unut time
N is av events in time t

SNR = mean/std dev = N/sqrt(N) = sqrt(N)

quality of data improves as sqrt(number of counts) : only if systematic etc error << 
So not linear

1sigma error bars for astronomy

Think pair share
Uncertainties in measurement
Uncertainties in location (distance)
Uncertainty in time
How many times do you repeat the measurement?
What instrument are you using?
Taking a video and going by millisecond?
Snapshots? - shutterspeed
Only a stopwatch - reaction time, perception


Speed will also have an uncertainty
Speed = distance/time

