Problem 3
AI prompt into google AI:
python code using numpy (no loops) to draw 10 times, 10 random samples from a 
gaussian distribution with mean 55 and standard deviation 13. Then create an 
array shape 10x3 with each row containing sample number (0-9), mean of each 
sample and standard deviation of each sample.

Resulting code:

import numpy as np

# 1. Initialize the random number generator and draw the samples
rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=42)  # Recommended way to handle randomness in modern NumPy

# Draw 10 times, 10 samples each, from a normal distribution
# This creates a 10x10 matrix where each row represents one sample trial
samples = rng.normal(loc=55, scale=13, size=(10, 10))

# 2. Calculate statistics for each row (axis=1) without using loops
sample_numbers = np.arange(10).reshape(-1, 1)  # Array of shapes [[0], [1], ..., [9]]
means = np.mean(samples, axis=1).reshape(-1, 1)
stds = np.std(samples, axis=1).reshape(-1, 1)

# 3. Stack the columns together horizontally to form a 10x3 summary array
summary_array = np.hstack((sample_numbers, means, stds))

# Display the final 10x3 array
print("Final 10x3 Summary Array (Sample Number, Mean, Std Dev):")
print(summary_array)

